  "interpretation": "Classes separated by structure - RSA keys and ECDSA signatures (ASN.1 DER framing), digests (fixed length), 3DES (8-byte block alignment), plaintext, base64 and compressed data - are classified near-perfectly. AES-GCM and ChaCha20 are confused with each other at close to chance, and this is the expected and correct result: both produce unpadded output that is indistinguishable from random by design. A randomness test that could separate them would constitute a distinguishing attack on the cipher. The SP 800-22 battery therefore answers 'is this cryptographic output', while the structural features answer 'which primitive produced it'."
